[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Device assignment

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-DEVICE-01
TITLE: Transient device attachment
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall attach a device to a qube for the lifetime of that
qube's current run.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Salt, QubesadminTools
RATIONALE: >>>
An attachment does not survive a restart, so it is an operation rather than
declarable state; the Ansible collection deliberately manages assignments only.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_device_attach

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-DEVICE-02
TITLE: Persistent device assignment
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall assign a device to a qube so that the assignment
survives a restart of that qube.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_device_assign

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-DEVICE-03
TITLE: Device assignment modes
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall set a device assignment's mode to ask-to-attach,
auto-attach or required.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_device_set_required

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-DEVICE-04
TITLE: PCI assignment constraint
STATEMENT: >>>
If a PCI device is bound to a qube, then the management tool shall record it as
a required assignment rather than an attachment.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Unwanted-behaviour
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
PCI passthrough is fixed at qube start, so any weaker binding leaves the qube
running without the device it was configured to have.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_device_assign

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Network and firewall

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-NET-01
TITLE: Netvm validation
STATEMENT: >>>
If the qube named as netvm does not provide network, then the management tool
shall reject the change.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Unwanted-behaviour
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_property_set

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-NET-02
TITLE: Firewall rule set
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall apply an ordered set of firewall rules to a qube,
replacing the rules previously in force.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
Rules are evaluated in order and the first match wins, so a rule set is only
meaningful as a whole sequence.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_firewall_set

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Convergence

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-CONV-01
TITLE: Idempotent application
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall make no change to a qube that already matches the
declared desired state.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-CONV-02
TITLE: Change reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall report, for each managed object, whether the run
changed it.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OBSERVABILITY
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-CONV-03
TITLE: Dry-run preview
STATEMENT: >>>
Where a dry run is requested, the management tool shall report the changes it
would make without applying any of them.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Optional-feature
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
A preview that mutates state is worse than no preview, because the
administrator acts on the assumption that nothing happened.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OBSERVABILITY
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-CONV-04
TITLE: Dependency-ordered application
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall apply changes in an order that satisfies the
dependencies between the qubes being configured.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-CONV-05
TITLE: Precondition validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall validate the declared desired state before applying
any part of it.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
A run that fails halfway leaves the system in a state that is neither the
previous one nor the declared one.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-CONV-06
TITLE: Drift detection
STATEMENT: >>>
When a managed object's live configuration differs from the recorded state, the management tool
shall report that difference in the change preview.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Event-driven
PRODUCT: Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OBSERVABILITY
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-CONV-07
TITLE: Drift correction
STATEMENT: >>>
When a managed qube was changed or removed outside the tool, the management tool shall restore its
declared state on the next run.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Event-driven
PRODUCT: Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-CONV-08
TITLE: Failed-creation rollback
STATEMENT: >>>
If creating a qube fails, then the management tool shall remove only objects that the failed run
itself created.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Unwanted-behaviour
PRODUCT: Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
A rollback that deletes a pre-existing qube destroys data the run never owned.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines

