[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Command execution

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-EXEC-01
TITLE: Command execution in qube
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall run a caller-supplied command inside a qube and
return that command's exit status.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-EXEC-02
TITLE: File transfer
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall transfer a file between the qube it is running in and the one being managed.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-EXEC-03
TITLE: Execution user selection
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall run a command in a qube under a caller-specified user
account.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
Running as root where the unprivileged user suffices widens the blast radius of
a compromised or malicious guest command.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Software and templates

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SW-02
TITLE: Template installation
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall install a template from a configured template
repository.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SW-03
TITLE: Template signature verification
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall verify the cryptographic signature of a downloaded
template before installing it.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
Template packages are unpacked in a management qube, so an unverified download
is a direct management qube code-execution path.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

