STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall provide functionality to update packages installed in dom0.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SYSTEM-05
TITLE: qrexec policy management
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall bring a named qrexec policy file to the rules given in the desired state.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SYSTEM-06
TITLE: Backup encryption
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall encrypt every backup it creates under a key derived
from a caller-supplied passphrase.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: QubesadminTools
RATIONALE: >>>
A backup leaves dom0's trust boundary as soon as it is written, so its
confidentiality cannot depend on where it is stored.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-IDEMPOTENT
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.backup_execute

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SYSTEM-07
TITLE: Backup integrity verification
STATEMENT: >>>
If a backup's integrity check fails, then the management tool shall abort the
restore without writing the affected data.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Unwanted-behaviour
PRODUCT: QubesadminTools
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SYSTEM-08
TITLE: Paranoid restore isolation
STATEMENT: >>>
Where a paranoid restore is requested, the management tool shall parse the
backup inside a DisposableVM rather than in dom0.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Optional-feature
PRODUCT: QubesadminTools
RATIONALE: >>>
A backup archive is attacker-controlled input if the machine that produced it
is not trusted.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Security and isolation

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SEC-01
TITLE: Untrusted data confinement
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall not interpret data originating from a managed qube.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SEC-02
TITLE: Management DisposableVM isolation
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall carry out a target's configuration work inside a
DisposableVM dedicated to that target.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt
RATIONALE: >>>
A DisposableVM shared between targets would let one managed qube observe or
influence the configuration of another.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_create

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SEC-03
TITLE: Management policy lifetime
STATEMENT: >>>
When a management run over a target ends, the management tool shall revoke the
administrative policy granted for that target.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Event-driven
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SEC-04
TITLE: Output sanitisation
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall sanitise text received from a managed qube before
writing it to a dom0 terminal.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt
RATIONALE: >>>
Terminal escape sequences in qube-supplied output are an injection path into
the administrator's dom0 session.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-SEC-05
TITLE: DisposableVM bypass prevention
STATEMENT: >>>
If a run is configured to bypass the management DisposableVM, then the
management tool shall refuse to start that run.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Unwanted-behaviour
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt
RATIONALE: >>>
The isolation boundary is only worth anything if it cannot be turned off by a
configuration setting the administrator may not have reviewed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Diagnostics

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-DIAG-01
TITLE: Failure exit status
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall exit with a non-zero status when any requested
operation fails.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OBSERVABILITY
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-DIAG-02
TITLE: Error attribution
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall attribute each reported failure to the qube and the
operation that produced it.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OBSERVABILITY
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2-DIAG-03
TITLE: Diagnostic verbosity control
STATEMENT: >>>
Where increased verbosity is requested, the management tool shall emit
additional detail about each operation it performs.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Optional-feature
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesadminTools, Terraform
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OBSERVABILITY
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]
